============================================================
Step 5: Physical interpretation of generators
============================================================
  Each generator is a direction in log-space along which Pi is preserved.
  Physically: simultaneous rescaling of variables that keeps the
  normalised enthalpy Pi (and therefore the pore fraction) invariant.

  Generator 1:
    P x exp(-0.455*eps), V x exp(+0.885*eps), Tm_minus_T0 x exp(-0.063*eps)
    Meaning: increase V while decrease P, decrease Tm_minus_T0
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 2:
    P x exp(-0.080*eps), A x exp(+0.996*eps)
    Meaning: increase A while decrease P
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 3:
    rho x exp(+0.999*eps)

  Generator 4:
    P x exp(-0.185*eps), k x exp(+0.981*eps)
    Meaning: increase k while decrease P
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 5:
    Lv x exp(+0.999*eps)

  Generator 6:
    P x exp(-0.052*eps), dT x exp(+0.998*eps)
    Meaning: increase dT while decrease P
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 7:
    P x exp(+0.096*eps), gamma x exp(+0.995*eps)
    Meaning: increase gamma while increase P
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 8:
    P x exp(-0.192*eps), Tb x exp(+0.980*eps)
    Meaning: increase Tb while decrease P
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged

  Generator 9:
    P x exp(-0.247*eps), V x exp(-0.063*eps), Tm_minus_T0 x exp(+0.966*eps)
    Meaning: increase Tm_minus_T0 while decrease P, decrease V
             to keep Pi (and pore fraction) unchanged


